    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **69 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the welcome-notification enqueue on successful owner create.\n\n**New function class** \u2014 `EnqueueWelcomeNotification.java`:\n- Emits `NOTIFY.info(\"welcome owner id={} memberId={}\", owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId())` via `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"NOTIFY\")`.\n- Reads the owner via `@Val Owner`, following the same OfficeFloor function-injection pattern as the neighboring `AuditOwnerCreated`.\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted a `welcome` step after `auditEvent` (so the owner already has its persisted id from `SaveOwner` and its `memberId` from `AssignMemberId`) and before `recordIdempotency`, keeping it under `govern: [ transaction ]` like the surrounding steps.\n\nThe new `Cp57Tests` (which captures the `NOTIFY` logger and asserts a line contains both the owner id and memberId) passes, and no existing tests regressed.",
